 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** Neighbor access for gradient computation must handle volume boundaries [G]. Standard clamping or reflection is assumed.
-*   **Precision:** The method relies on quantization of gradients; the specific quantization error is not discussed, but the finite set size impacts shading quality [S1, book].
+*   **Hardware Realization:** The architecture is designed to be simple and suitable for hardware realization [S2, book].
+*   **Precision:** The method relies on a finite set of local gradients, which may limit the accuracy of surface orientation representation compared to continuous normal fields [S2, book].
 
